WEBVTT

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:09.420
In 2291, Slipspace technology
makes space colonization a reality.

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:13.670
In 30 years,
mankind establishes the Inner Colonies...

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:15.550
...in the heart of the Milky Way...

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:19.890
...and soon into the outer periphery.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:27.230
In the year 2525, the human race
encounters an advanced alien alliance.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:32.070
This alliance called itself the Covenant.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:36.700
The Covenant decrees humanity
an affront to their gods...

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:40.910
...and the Human-Covenant War begins.

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:46.040
Within a decade, the Outer Colonies
are almost completely annihilated...

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:48.250
...by the power of the Covenant.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:53.550
In the face of direct attacks on the
Inner Colonies by Covenant forces...

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:56.220
...humanity's only remaining hope...

00:00:56.380 --> 00:01:01.640
...depends on a special unit
of genetically-augmented soldiers.

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:06.940
These soldiers were known
as the Spartan-lls.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:20.950
They finally decide to give the order
to pull out and now this.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.040
Damn it. It just ain't my day.

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:27.210
Mac, watch out!

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:33.250
Here they come.

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:55.230
Oh, damn it. This just ain't my day.

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:09.750
What the hell?

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:28.180
Maybe this is my day.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:32.150
All right, men. Let's welcome
our chief petty officer with some backup.

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:56.040
And stay down.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:08.060
How's Gamma-4?

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:09.890
Gamma-4 is gone.

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:13.400
Then that means this planet is finished.

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:15.860
And it won't be the last, sir.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:18.400
I have the main unit on the line.

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:20.740
Rescue team will be in accordance...

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:24.070
...with the order to fully disengage.
Dispatching a rescue craft.

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:27.240
All active units respond immediately.

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:32.710
Team Gamma here, roger that.
We are completely surrounded.

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:33.920
Copy that, marine.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.340
We're dispatching a rescue ship
to your location.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:39.210
But I'm afraid we can't
exactly give you curbside service.

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:43.090
Sending coordinates for extraction point.
You're going to have to make your way...

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:44.840
- Wait a sec.
- What?

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:48.220
I know that voice. Is that you?

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:51.730
Daisy. That's you, isn't it?

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:56.650
Ralph.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:03.950
- Where do we go now?
- I don't know.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:06.030
- Anywhere but that place.
- Yeah.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:09.740
I don't wanna think about
what they'd do to us if we did go back.

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:13.210
We're not gonna be your toys anymore.

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:15.960
She's right. We're sick of your training.

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:19.960
We're leaving and you can't stop us.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:27.800
What would our moms and dads
think of us if they saw us?

00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:30.100
It's been seven years.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:32.470
I wonder if they'd recognize us.

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:35.980
Not because we've grown up
but because of what's been done to us.

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:38.360
All of those years of training.

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:41.610
All those horrible surgeries
and the augmentations.

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:45.150
But everything's changed now.
And not just us.

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:47.320
You really think you can go home?

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:50.830
It doesn't matter. I'm going. I have to.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:53.160
It's the only home that I have.

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:55.870
I guess tomorrow is goodbye then.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:00.750
We won't be able
to see each other anymore, will we?

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:06.840
Of the five escapees from the facility...

00:05:07.010 --> 00:05:08.840
...only subject Joseph-122
has been captured.

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:11.850
The search for the other four
is a Priority-Red directive.

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:15.850
Repeat. The search for the other four
is a Priority-Red directive.

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:45.670
Not again. I'm getting off this rock.

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:48.050
And I'm not going home
in a body bag either.

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:51.180
I'm gonna create a diversion. Keep low.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:54.060
You make a run for the extraction point.

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:03.380
Jesus, they're everywhere.

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:07.000
All the more reason for us to move
as soon as we see the extraction craft.

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:11.510
That sounds like a good idea to me.
I'm gonna go find us a Hog.

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:31.210
Don't you dare slow down.
Heads up.

00:08:32.670 --> 00:08:34.510
You okay down there?

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:36.220
They're here.

00:09:12.590 --> 00:09:15.260
Notice any resemblance?

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:20.140
The secrecy of the Spartan-ll program
could not be jeopardized.

00:09:20.300 --> 00:09:22.890
But the disappearance
of 75 recruits for the program...

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:24.930
...would've created difficult questions.

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:28.100
But if the children never vanished...

00:09:28.270 --> 00:09:31.860
...there would be no questions to ask,
would there?

00:09:32.020 --> 00:09:34.730
The clone lives a life in your place...

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:39.490
...the life that was originally meant
for you.

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:42.120
Come back to the facility, 23.

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:47.290
It is where you belong. It's home.

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:08.350
Sarge, are you all right?

00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:13.480
I will be as soon as we're out of here.

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:16.070
Look, I'll cover you. Go on ahead.

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:18.450
- There's no way I'm leaving...
- Just go. Now.

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:19.900
Step on it.

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:23.910
Let's go.

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:54.810
Huh?

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:02.660
Faster, faster!

00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:01.210
- Daisy!
- Chief!

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:11.930
I'm coming. Stay right there.

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:15.600
There's no time. Go, Ralph.

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:17.440
Get that ship out of here now.

00:12:53.430 --> 00:12:56.310
Sometimes I have this dream.

00:12:58.690 --> 00:13:00.190
Always the same dream.

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:04.320
I dream I'm strong.
Stronger than anyone.

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:07.990
Like you. Just like you are.

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:11.580
Here. I want you to have this.

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:21.590
But why me?

00:13:23.170 --> 00:13:25.420
I don't know, to be honest with you.

00:13:25.590 --> 00:13:28.510
I just... Something tells me that I should.

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:29.930
I want you to take it.

00:13:46.450 --> 00:13:50.030
My clone. He was... He was sick.

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:52.530
I think I killed him.

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:55.540
Don't do this to yourself, Ralph.

00:13:55.700 --> 00:13:58.920
You did what you had to do.

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:00.580
So did I.

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:01.960
Daisy?

00:14:03.550 --> 00:14:04.710
Transport to base.

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:08.220
Custody of Daisy-23
and Ralph-303 restored.

00:14:08.380 --> 00:14:12.510
Subject's ETA, one hour.
After making contact with their clones...

00:14:12.680 --> 00:14:16.890
...the remaining two escapees
used their small arms to commit suicide.

00:15:44.980 --> 00:15:48.440
This is Charlie-1.
Sending new rendezvous coordinates.

00:15:48.610 --> 00:15:50.900
Prepare to disengage.
